  "structural_change": "v15 successor of the retired flat hfd_lk_ep (13 failed routes): one ~8k-flop master for all 9 ep windows, lane gearbox 613b->512b fixed 4-in-5 format + off-die elastic RX pingpong (0az boundary), every port pin-registered, one clock root. Route-2 fix of route-1 EARLY_FAIL_HOLD (setup/hold conflict at enable-mux D pins with one 612-load select): selects replicated per 64-b slice, bypass-free SRAM leaf, macro columns facing one centre datapath channel, logic band at the COLL/SerDes faces. Route-3 fix of route-2 EARLY_FAIL_CONGESTION (12 zero-capacity M2/M4 gcells on 3 nets at the inward SRAM faces of the 47 um centre channel; abutted N-S macro pairs left no horizontal corridor): the two macro rows are separated by a 21.6 um horizontal channel (outline 434.72 x 315.36 inside the 434.72 x 515.2 window), giving the face escapes and the band->channel nets a crossing corridor. Route-4 native fix (route 3 CLOSED TT +128.49 / FF +7.69 but native launch 223.2 ps on 3 sd_tx pins, capture 212.7 ps on sd_rx[1]): sd_rx[1] (SerDes IDLE bit) loads ONE pin flop (it fed 9), the per-slice data copies and the RX gearbox beat move one edge later (+1 RX cycle at the off-die boundary, +520 flops); clk entry moved west on the S face to x 151.2-153.36 um (between tx_frame and the controls) to cut the late W-face boundary arrival. Route-5 fix of route-4 native FAIL (launch 259.7 on 25 sd_tx pins at W y 2-8, capture 221.3 on tx_frame S x 16-19; R 429.6 spread 100.8): SW corner pin-flop crowding where the W SerDes and S COLL pin-flop fields meet -> 19.44 um corner keep-out on both faces, sd_tx 512 pins over 77.8 um (6.6/um, was 7.5), S pins shifted +19.44 um (rx_pin unchanged); same RTL, same outline. Route-5b (parallel to route 5 bc6c91699): route-5 gate showed the sd_rx pin flops squeezed into the 17 um W channel beside the lower-left macro (red strip); both macro rows move N by 56.16 um (outline 434.72 x 371.52, inside the 434.72 x 515.2 window) so the whole W SerDes pin field (y 21.6-172.8) faces the logic band, not a macro. Route-5d (5b outline/pins/RTL): route 5b native capture FAIL 213.6 on 517 inputs; each input path carries the kit pad (HB2+BUFx4f) plus 2-4 route hold buffers (netlist: tx_frame[47] -> HB2 -> BUFx4f -> HB2 -> 3x BUFx2 -> p_tx_f D), and FF input->reg hold slack is +35.6 ps (pre-ECO +20.1): the inputs are over-padded for hold. Fix: route hold margin 30 -> 10 ps and no kit input hold pad (repair sizes input hold itself). | 5e (H-LKEP 1315, 10-16): 5d kit + output hold pad HB1xp67 (was HB2) on the leaf_iohold output stage; target native launch <= 215 with capture <= 190 (5d 186.8, no input pad). Same RTL, outline 434.72 x 371.52, pins. | 5f (H-LKEP 1815, 10-16): 5e kit/RTL/outline/pins unchanged; post-route hold ECO goal 18 -> 5 ps (spec job.hold_eco.hold_margin_ps). 5e native capture FAIL 215.76 on 234 inputs was ECO over-padding: pre-ECO FF -7.74 (109 endpoints), the 2-pass ECO repaired 5478 endpoints to target 35.1 and put 213 ps of hold cells on each tx_frame capture path; a source-exact removal screen (Codex 5480fc55e) shows the inputs need <=~35 ps FF hold for capture <=190.",
